<title>HONG KONG: HK to sell note printer interest to Chinese bank.</title>
<headline>HK to sell note printer interest to Chinese bank.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) said on Wednesday the government has entered into an agreement to sell a 15 percent stake in the territory's banknote printing firm to a unit of China's central bank.</p>
<p>The government agreed to sell 3.83 million ordinary shares, or 15 percent, of its Hong Kong Note Printing Ltd for HK$42.5 million to China Banknote Printing and Minting Corp, the HKMA said in a statement.</p>
<p>The latter is a subsidiary of the People's Bank of China responsible for the printing and minting of Chinese currency.</p>
<p>Britain hands the colony back to China on July 1, ending more than 150 years of colonial rule.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
